            "paragraph": "The outlook is bright for a continuing improvement in our understanding of the oceanic water cycle due to the development of a series of new salinity observing technologies and platforms. Along with the existing Argo float array, two new satellite platforms have begun to provide near-global-ocean surface salinity observations. The Soil Moisture and Ocean Salinity (SMOS; Berger et al., 2002) platform was launched in November 2009, and the dedicated surface salinity satellite Aquarius (Lagerloef et al., 2008) was launched in June 2011.",
